# Panel 180 R5, shape 24 of the compiler-engineer's 117 (call args): a break
# before , (after an operator).
# By the spec's opening paragraph, the line ends with `1`, a literal, so it
# keeps its NEWLINE, which may stand before a `,`, and in a list the two are
# one separator: accepted, exit 0.
function shape()
    f(a: 1
        , b: 2)
